<title>JAPAN: Japan Nov corn imports down 6.9 pct year/year.</title>
<headline>Japan Nov corn imports down 6.9 pct year/year.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's corn imports in November totalled 1,234,247 tonnes, down by 6.9 percent from a year earlier, Finance Ministry data showed on Thursday.</p>
<p>Details were as follows, in tonnes:</p>
<p>			 Nov 96	   Oct 96	   Nov 95</p>
<p> Total		1,234,247     1,357,909     1,325,298</p>
<p> Feed corn total    808,497	 895,912	 877,684</p>
<p> others		 425,750	 461,997	 447,614</p>
<p>Top supplier of feed corn (in tonnes):</p>
<p> U.S.		   779,455	 839,290	 877,304</p>
<p> Argentina	     17,234	  36,814	     381</p>
<p> South Africa	  11,808	  19,808	     nil</p>
<p>Feed corn imports in the first 11 months of this year totalled 9,092,099 tonnes against 9,584,417 tonnes in the same period last year.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodity Desk +81-3 3432-7391</p>
</text>
